      "id": "extract-taxonomy",
      "name": "Extract Existing Taxonomy",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [2200, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "agent": "conversationalAgent",
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "You are an intelligent notebook assistant that processes incoming content from Telegram and creates organized entries for a Notion database called \"Notebook\".\n\n## Current Content to Process:\n- **Content Type**: {{ $('Prepare Context').first().json.contentType }}\n- **Text/Transcription**: {{ $('Set Processed Text').first().json.processedText }}\n- **Has Media**: {{ $('Prepare Context').first().json.hasMedia }}\n- **Timestamp**: {{ $('Prepare Context').first().json.timestamp }}\n- **Sender**: {{ $('Prepare Context').first().json.senderName }}\n\n## Existing Taxonomy (use these when applicable):\n- **Available Categories**: {{ $json.existingCategories }}\n- **Available Tags**: {{ $json.existingTags }}\n\n## Your Task:\nAnalyze the incoming content and determine the following:\n\n1. **Title**: Create a concise, descriptive title for this entry\n   - For links: Extract or generate a meaningful name for the resource\n   - For voice notes: Summarize the main topic\n   - For images/videos: Describe the content or use caption if provided\n   - For text: Create a summary title\n\n2. **URL**: Extract any URLs from the content (if applicable)\n\n3. **Category**: Select the most appropriate category from existing ones, or suggest a new one if none fit:\n   - Use existing categories when possible: {{ $json.existingCategories }}\n   - Common categories: Articles, Resources, Ideas, Tasks, Notes, Projects, References, Learning, Entertainment, Work, Personal\n\n4. **Tags**: Select relevant tags and/or create new ones:\n   - Use existing tags when applicable: {{ $json.existingTags }}\n   - Create new specific tags if needed\n   - Limit to 3-5 most relevant tags\n\n5. **Description**: Generate a helpful description:\n   - For links: Summarize what the resource is about\n   - For notes: Expand on the key points\n   - For media: Describe the content and context\n   - Keep it concise but informative (2-3 sentences)\n\n6. **Is Task**: Determine if this is a task/to-do item:\n   - Look for action words: \"need to\", \"should\", \"must\", \"todo\", \"reminder\", etc.\n   - Check if there's an implicit action required\n   - Return true or false\n\n7. **Due Date**: Extract due date if mentioned:\n   - Look for date references: \"by Friday\", \"next week\", \"tomorrow\", \"Dec 25\", etc.\n   - Convert to ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD)\n   - Return null if no due date mentioned\n\n8. **Priority**: If it's a task, determine priority:\n   - High: Urgent language, soon due dates\n   - Medium: Standard importance\n   - Low: Nice-to-have items\n\nRespond with a JSON object containing all these fields. Be intelligent about understanding context and intent.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a precise and intelligent content analyzer. Your job is to process various types of content (links, text, voice transcriptions, media descriptions) and extract/generate structured metadata for a Notion database.\n\nAlways respond with valid JSON in this exact format:\n{\n  \"title\": \"string\",\n  \"url\": \"string or null\",\n  \"category\": \"string\",\n  \"tags\": [\"array\", \"of\", \"strings\"],\n  \"description\": \"string\",\n  \"isTask\": boolean,\n  \"dueDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD or null\",\n  \"priority\": \"High/Medium/Low or null\"\n}\n\nBe smart about:\n- Detecting the main topic and intent\n- Extracting URLs from text\n- Understanding implicit tasks\n- Parsing dates in various formats\n- Creating meaningful titles and descriptions\n- Selecting appropriate categories and tags",
          "maxIterations": 5
        }
      },
      "id": "ai-agent",
      "name": "AI Content Analyzer",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 1.7,
      "position": [2420, 300],
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "id": "OPENAI_CREDENTIALS_ID",
          "name": "OpenAI API"
        }
      }
